WEBVTT

00:03:28.389 --> 00:03:30.473
your lexicon swells with phrases like

00:03:30.473 --> 00:03:33.519
"devoured alive" and "bursts out of its body."

00:03:33.519 --> 00:03:34.756
(Laughter)

00:03:34.756 --> 00:03:36.296
But there's more to it than that.

00:03:36.296 --> 00:03:38.398
I'm a writer, and fellow writers in the audience

00:03:38.398 --> 00:03:41.107
will know that we love stories.

00:03:41.107 --> 00:03:43.500
Parasites invite us to resist the allure

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.350
of obvious stories.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:47.660
Their world is one of plot twists

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:51.267
and unexpected explanations.

00:03:51.267 --> 00:03:52.763
Why, for example,

00:03:52.763 --> 00:03:54.941
does this caterpillar

00:03:54.941 --> 00:03:56.915
start violently thrashing about

00:03:56.915 --> 00:03:58.583
when another insect gets close to it

00:03:58.583 --> 00:04:00.840
and those white cocoons that it seems